# DEBT-0021: Over-Broad Tool Authority in Session Tool Allow-List

## 1. Context
To resolve DEBT-0019, `"Bash"` was added to `_allowed_tools()` in `runtime/integrations/__init__.py`.

## 2. Problem & Risk
`_allowed_tools()` applies to all sub-sessions (`Role.PLANNER`, `Role.DESIGNER`, `Role.BUILDER`). Consequently, `PLANNER` and `DESIGNER` sessions receive `Bash` execution authority, violating the Principle of Least Privilege (FP-7 / Separation of Powers). Only `BUILDER` sessions require `Bash` to run reproduction commands for Court evidence.

## 3. Recommended Resolution
Refactor `_allowed_tools(package: TaskPackage)` to inspect `package.role` (or permission spec) and restrict `Bash` strictly to `Role.BUILDER` sessions.

## 4. Status
**RESOLVED** (2026-08-04). `_allowed_tools()` in `runtime/integrations/__init__.py` now appends
`"Bash"` only when `package.role is Role.BUILDER`; PLANNER/DESIGN sessions retain least privilege
(Read/Write/Edit + scoped MCP, no command execution). Covered by
`tests/runtime/test_live_adapter.py::test_builder_allow_list_contains_bash` and
`::test_planner_allow_list_omits_bash_least_privilege`.
